    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2+y^2=1$, excluding $(0,-1)$.\n\nSquare and add the coordinates; $y+1=\\dfrac{2}{1+t^2}>0$ excludes that point.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+y^2&=\\frac{4t^2+(1-t^2)^2}{(1+t^2)^2}\\\\x^2+y^2&=\\frac{1+2t^2+t^4}{(1+t^2)^2}\\\\x^2+y^2&=1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince\n\n$$y+1=\\frac{2}{1+t^2}>0,$$\n\n$y\\ne-1$, so $(0,-1)$ is excluded. For any other point on the circle, $t=\\dfrac{x}{1+y}$ recovers the original coordinates. Hence the curve is $x^2+y^2=1$, excluding $(0,-1)$ only.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
